/* ---- perf5_terrain (2026-11-03): the terrain overlay passes' triangles that cannot change a pixel ----
   perf5_merge measured the world's GPU time as the terrain's pixels: M3 0.91 ms a drawing, of it ~0.57 the overlay pass
   3 (a world-XZ layer read from a render target, ~1,000 draws a frame) and 0.094 the detail passes 1-2. Every overlay
   pass (block program 1, pass 1-3) blends Cd - Cs x FIX (GS 0x162, FIX 128) with MODULATE, no fog, no depth or alpha
   write: where the source colour is 0 the pass leaves the frame exactly as it is. Its vertex colour is 0 beyond the
   game's fade distance (passes 1-2: the detail fade; pass 3: the fog value, colour = F / 2).
   PS2_PERF_TERRAIN_ZCULL=1 (default; 0 = mesh.vert as before): every native mesh draws with mesh.vert's variant
   mesh_zc*.vert.spv (-DZCULL: one vertex program for all the terrain's passes, as before), which culls the triangles of
   a marked draw whose three vertices give the texture function rgb 0 (gl_CullDistance; zc_zero there). A draw is
   marked (push-constant bit TZC_BIT of mesh_pad) only when its blend leaves the target as it is for a source colour
   of 0 (tzc_gate: D = Cd, A / B = Cs and 0, blending on; no depth, alpha or float-target write; not the channel
   shuffle; no debug colour). Exact: the culled triangles' fragments all have rgb 0, every other fragment is drawn as
   before. Needs the device's shaderCullDistance (else off, logged). PS2_PASS_AB_WHAT=terrzc: GPU A/B, the "off" blocks
   as before the switch (no marks, and every native mesh with mesh.vert itself: pipeline key bit 61); PS2_PERF_AB_FLIP=
   terrzc: the same-frame re-draw as before it (the exact image check of the whole change, the vertex program too).
   Measured and left out (the code: a private script): skipping pass 3's quads
   whose filter footprint lies in zero cells of a GPU-built mask of the layer, before the fetch. Exact (same-frame and
   gsreplay images identical), catches a median 57 % of M3's pass-3 fragments, and is a net loss: +0.258 +- 0.034 ms a
   game frame (two drawings); the split between the mask's build, the per-fragment test and the fetches saved was not
   measured.
   PS2_TERRAIN_ZCENSUS=N (diagnostic, seconds between log lines; needs fragmentStoresAndAtomics): the native terrain's
   draws take the fragment shaders' census variants (mesh_zcen*, gs_zcen*: terrain_zcensus.glsl), which count each
   pass's fragments by what they can still contribute into the reserved mesh blocks ZC_BLOCK0..+1 (the frame's arena
   stops below them); `terrain-zc:` lines per pass: fragments a frame, reached the output, vertex colour 0, texel 0,
   exact no-op, no-op by rounding only, texel 0 under a non-zero colour. With BENCH_REPEAT=K a frame counts K drawings. */
#define TZC_BIT 134217728u                     /* mesh.vert: the draw may cull its zero-colour triangles (1 << 27) */
#define ZC_BLOCK0 15864u                       /* the census counters (terrain_zcensus.glsl ZC_BLOCK0) */
#define ZC_N (8u * 4u * 7u)                    /* 8 copies x 4 passes x 7 categories (u32) */
static int tzc_ok;                             /* PS2_PERF_TERRAIN_ZCULL on, cull distances enabled, the variant loaded */
static int zcen_ok;                            /* PS2_TERRAIN_ZCENSUS on, fragment atomics enabled, its variants loaded */
static VkShaderModule zcen_mesh_fs, zcen_gs_fs, zcen_gs_lr_fs;
